  "finalText": "The NOVA logo reveal is built in the Main comp (4 s, 60 fps, navy background). I went with the **Cut** concept: the ring draws on, then the accent slash strikes through it as the circle closes.\n\n- **Mark ring** draws on from 0.1 s (Sine In Out, 0.8 s).\n- **Mark slash** (mint `#3DDC97`, the only accent) cuts through the ring from 0.75 s (Expo Out, 0.45 s).\n- **Wordmark NOVA** sits in a clipping group at the mark's edge. It starts fully hidden behind the mark, slides out from 1.2 s (Quart Out, 0.9 s), and has a 6% settle.\n- **Tagline \"Money, made simple\"** sits below the ring, fades in from 2.2 s and rises 12 px (Sine Out, 0.6 s).\n- **Hold** of the full lockup runs from about 2.8 s to 4 s, with no motion.\n\nCritique scores the piece 93/100. The one remaining note is that most elements move once and stop, which I left as is for a calm, precise feel. The ring/slash overlap it flags is intentional. Tell me if you want the mark to have a settle or a subtle breathing move during the hold.\n\nI can also build the Assemble or Ignite concept instead, or change the accent color."
